From: Hummingbird <hummingbird@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Sync go.mod/go.sum with go-vendor-tools.toml pre_commands

go-vendor-tools.toml's [archive] pre_commands mutate go.mod (remove
modernc.org/sqlite, then `go get` bump moby/buildkit, golang.org/x/text,
and sigstore/sigstore-go for CVE fixes) before the vendor archive is
generated -- but those commands only ever run against gorget's own
fetch/vendor checkout, never against the actual %prep source tree. The
existing %prep sed here only replicates the code-level sqlite import
swap, not the go.mod-level changes, so go.mod in the build tree and
vendor/modules.txt in the vendor archive disagree on golang.org/x/net
and golang.org/x/text's versions (x/crypto too, as a side effect of the
x/text bump shifting MVS resolution) -- `go build -mod=vendor` rejects
this as inconsistent vendoring.

%prep can't just run the pre_commands' `go get` calls directly: Konflux
builds hermetically, with no network access, so this patch captures the
exact go.mod/go.sum result of running go-vendor-tools.toml's pre_commands
(offline, ahead of time) as static content instead, keeping %prep purely
textual like the sed above it.

